00:09:09.882 --> 00:09:11.972
Delwath: Well, I rolled a 20. You got a 31.

00:09:11.972 --> 00:09:15.492
Wellby: Which is great. You literally just made that up.

00:09:15.492 --> 00:09:15.521
Unknown: [laughs]

00:09:15.521 --> 00:09:15.772
Kenzo: [laughs]

00:09:15.772 --> 00:09:18.942
Wellby: And no one is gonna say anything about it.

00:09:18.942 --> 00:09:19.012
Unknown: [laughs]

00:09:19.012 --> 00:09:19.692
DM: Wow.

00:09:20.952 --> 00:09:22.212
Unknown: It was a good number.

00:09:22.212 --> 00:09:25.052
Unknown: It was well.

00:09:25.052 --> 00:09:25.332
DM: [coughs]

00:09:25.332 --> 00:09:26.532
Kenzo: [laughs]

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:29.172
DM: I thought you had rolled before you went to sit down on the couch.

00:09:29.172 --> 00:09:30.932
Unknown: That's true.

00:09:30.932 --> 00:09:32.792
Unknown: Maybe.

00:09:32.792 --> 00:09:33.252
Unknown: [laughs]

00:09:33.252 --> 00:09:33.852
DM: Um, in any case-

00:09:33.852 --> 00:09:34.792
Unknown: I thought that for a second.

00:09:36.492 --> 00:09:36.942
Unknown: I was like, "No." [laughs]

00:09:36.942 --> 00:09:37.432
Kenzo: No, you didn't.

00:09:39.772 --> 00:09:42.812
DM: You match the monk and begin sparring with it.

00:09:45.352 --> 00:09:45.662
DM: And

00:09:46.672 --> 00:09:47.162
DM: with the,

00:09:48.352 --> 00:09:49.952
DM: all of the monks here that are,

00:09:51.232 --> 00:09:55.892
DM: uh, pantomiming, you crash through the last barrier

00:09:57.592 --> 00:10:05.372
DM: with a retinue of monks who solidify into people as you cross into an open monastery,

00:10:07.332 --> 00:10:08.452
DM: uh, with a,

00:10:09.812 --> 00:10:10.172
DM: uh...

00:10:11.212 --> 00:10:14.832
DM: So it's like the cl- it's like the, a cloister, so there's, there's a,

00:10:16.092 --> 00:10:23.032
DM: an open courtyard, pretty big, a couple hundred feet across with this building in the center of it, a small dome building in the center of it.

00:10:25.012 --> 00:10:25.472
DM: The...

00:10:27.012 --> 00:10:32.892
DM: And then the, the cloisters have sort of, uh, a shaded extent that comes over and you can see that there's monks.

00:10:32.892 --> 00:10:34.012
DM: It's sandy in the middle,

00:10:35.432 --> 00:10:37.292
DM: um, but there's monks that are sweeping.

00:10:37.292 --> 00:10:41.372
DM: There's monks that are sort of doing walking circle meditations.

00:10:41.372 --> 00:10:45.792
DM: Everything that you see is, like, very repetitive and, um,

00:10:46.812 --> 00:10:49.752
DM: sort of strictly choreographed.

00:10:49.752 --> 00:11:00.132
DM: Uh, the n- the monks that, um, that are following you sort of stumble out, um, and, and look around, like, briefly awed and then

00:11:00.132 --> 00:11:03.571
DM: sort of quickly begin resuming tasks.

00:11:03.572 --> 00:11:13.952
DM: And as they, as they carry out these tasks, sweeping, praying, a couple of them are sparring, um, there's, there's some that look like they're, they're making

00:11:13.952 --> 00:11:15.912
DM: scrolls or writing something on paper.

00:11:17.372 --> 00:11:23.352
DM: Um, there's some that are, uh, you know, what looks like meal prep or something like that.

00:11:23.352 --> 00:11:33.842
DM: And as these, these monks that you rescued continue these activities, they start, they become more solid over time as they repeat these choreographed

00:11:33.842 --> 00:11:36.852
DM: behaviors. Like when they, when you first pull them through,

00:11:38.152 --> 00:11:39.392
DM: they're thin. They're sort of,

00:11:40.732 --> 00:11:44.722
DM: uh, desaturated and almost translucent, still sort of misty.

00:11:44.722 --> 00:11:46.372
Delwath: Is somebody making hot water?

00:11:46.372 --> 00:11:46.712
Unknown: Yes.

00:11:46.712 --> 00:11:54.632
DM: And as they begin to repeat these motions over and over, they begin to, like the flesh begins to solidify on them.

00:11:54.692 --> 00:11:57.071
Kenzo: It's like Back to the Future when that...

00:11:57.072 --> 00:11:57.792
Unknown: Mm-hmm.

00:11:57.792 --> 00:11:57.972
Kenzo: Yeah.

00:12:00.892 --> 00:12:04.912
DM: None of the monks seem to look like they're particularly interacting with-

00:12:05.832 --> 00:12:08.592
Kenzo: Are there, are there, the ones that are like coming back, are they kind of conscious?

00:12:08.592 --> 00:12:13.492
Kenzo: Are they like more, are their souls and consciousnesses like more normal?

00:12:14.612 --> 00:12:16.772
Kenzo: Or are they just like automatons?

00:12:16.772 --> 00:12:18.232
DM: No, no, no. They're, um,

00:12:19.312 --> 00:12:19.552
DM: uh...

00:12:21.792 --> 00:12:29.292
DM: What it feels like in Soul Sight is, is sort of like there's fuzz that's slowly melting away and revealing-

00:12:30.832 --> 00:12:35.732
Delwath: I wonder if they're the ones who like have faded, have like failed at being...

00:12:38.232 --> 00:12:41.772
Delwath: The ones who are outside are the ones who like didn't

00:12:43.032 --> 00:12:43.381
Delwath: s-

00:12:43.381 --> 00:12:43.381
Kenzo: Hmm

00:12:43.381 --> 00:12:45.592
Delwath: ... who like Limbo started to take, right?

00:12:45.592 --> 00:12:48.152
Kenzo: Oh, yeah. That was the whole implication, that the ones that we first interacted with-

00:12:48.152 --> 00:12:48.162
Delwath: Yeah

00:12:48.162 --> 00:12:49.572
Kenzo: ... were the most fucked up and destroyed.

00:12:49.572 --> 00:12:49.582
Delwath: Yeah, yeah.

00:12:49.582 --> 00:12:51.532
Kenzo: And the closer we are to the monastery, the more-

00:12:51.532 --> 00:12:51.972
Delwath: Hmm

00:12:51.972 --> 00:12:52.852
Kenzo: ... ordered they are.

00:12:52.852 --> 00:12:54.322
Delwath: Yeah.

00:12:54.322 --> 00:12:56.592
Unknown: It's, I mean, it, you, you, this is the...

00:12:56.592 --> 00:13:02.092
DM: I mean, the idea is that the more they, like, as they continue these kind of-

00:13:02.092 --> 00:13:02.292
Delwath: Yes

00:13:02.292 --> 00:13:04.832
DM: ... very structured behaviors-

00:13:04.832 --> 00:13:04.972
Delwath: Yeah, yeah

00:13:04.972 --> 00:13:07.192
DM: ... the kind of limbo fuzz begins-

00:13:07.192 --> 00:13:07.201
Delwath: Yeah

00:13:07.201 --> 00:13:08.352
DM: ... to melt away.

00:13:08.352 --> 00:13:08.712
Delwath: Yeah.

00:13:08.712 --> 00:13:10.732
DM: It, it would take some time for them, like-

00:13:11.792 --> 00:13:11.842
Delwath: Yeah

00:13:11.842 --> 00:13:15.832
DM: ... you still sense they're s- they're still kind of fuzzy, right?

00:13:15.832 --> 00:13:15.852
Delwath: Yeah.

00:13:15.852 --> 00:13:17.512
DM: But they're getting less fuzzy

00:13:18.932 --> 00:13:19.452
DM: as they-

00:13:19.452 --> 00:13:19.462
Kenzo: Cool

00:13:19.462 --> 00:13:21.392
DM: ... carry out these activities.

00:13:21.392 --> 00:13:21.912
Kenzo: Excellent.

00:13:23.972 --> 00:13:26.212
Delwath: Um, do we see a jade statue?

00:13:27.632 --> 00:13:30.032
DM: Well, the jade statue's in the building in the middle.

00:13:30.032 --> 00:13:31.612
Delwath: Ah, right. So let's-

00:13:31.612 --> 00:13:32.652
Kenzo: Yeah, let's go to the-

00:13:32.652 --> 00:13:32.672
Delwath: Shall we?

00:13:32.672 --> 00:13:33.592
Kenzo: Let's go

00:13:33.592 --> 00:13:34.972
Delwath: ... carefully avoiding the-

00:13:34.972 --> 00:13:35.602
Kenzo: I mean, we'll like-

00:13:35.602 --> 00:13:37.392
Seeker: ... geometries of the sweeping monks

00:13:37.392 --> 00:13:39.452
Delwath: ... st- let the pattern, like be very careful not to disturb the-

00:13:39.452 --> 00:13:41.112
DM: Right, not to disturb the pattern.

00:13:41.112 --> 00:13:41.712
DM: Yeah.

00:13:41.712 --> 00:13:44.052
Kenzo: We all walk synchronized, in lockstep.

00:13:44.052 --> 00:13:44.212
Delwath: Right.

00:13:44.212 --> 00:13:44.772
DM: Yeah.

00:13:44.772 --> 00:13:45.592
Kenzo: Actually, we should.

00:13:45.592 --> 00:13:46.332
Delwath: We shall.

00:13:46.332 --> 00:13:46.552
Kenzo: Yep.

00:13:49.092 --> 00:13:51.772
Delwath: Like we've never practiced marching before.

00:13:51.772 --> 00:13:53.052
Delwath: [laughs]

00:13:53.052 --> 00:13:57.932
DM: So as you approach this central building, the door swings open

00:13:59.712 --> 00:14:09.952
DM: by itself, and you can see inside, the interior is a nearly perfect copy of, although in smaller scale, of the Temple of the Eight Divines in Drankor.

00:14:09.952 --> 00:14:10.392
Kenzo: Whoa.

00:14:10.392 --> 00:14:10.412
Delwath: Oh.

00:14:10.412 --> 00:14:10.972
DM: Except

00:14:12.492 --> 00:14:17.872
DM: that the art has shifted, and it's now stories that, Kenzo, you recognize from...

00:14:17.872 --> 00:14:18.272
DM: And actually,

00:14:19.332 --> 00:14:22.162
DM: Seeker did like most of the Bhishma initiation, too.

00:14:22.162 --> 00:14:24.042
DM: It's like the stories from the-

00:14:24.042 --> 00:14:24.182
Delwath: Oh, yeah

00:14:24.182 --> 00:14:25.592
DM: ... Bhishma Temple that are now.

00:14:25.592 --> 00:14:27.352
Kenzo: You forgot that. Well, you're also... Yeah, that's right.

00:14:27.352 --> 00:14:32.861
DM: But Seeker didn't like accept the, you know, will you die and be resurrected thing.

00:14:32.861 --> 00:14:34.212
Delwath: Yeah. You did most of the ground up.

00:14:34.212 --> 00:14:34.852
DM: Um.

00:14:34.852 --> 00:14:35.032
Delwath: Right.

00:14:36.192 --> 00:14:40.812
DM: So it's like that, except the stories have been replaced by those stories, by the...

00:14:40.812 --> 00:14:50.992
DM: So there's like illuminated illustrations on the ceiling of, you know, Bhishma leading the, um, the Dunmari, of like Bhishma, um, pray, like leading everybody

00:14:50.992 --> 00:14:53.771
DM: in prayer, Jeevali being resurrected.

00:14:53.772 --> 00:15:01.452
DM: Kind of the story of the, you know, the death and rebirth that was the Festival of Rebirth at the very beginning of the campaign.

00:15:02.812 --> 00:15:09.012
Kenzo: Wait, and, uh, in Drankor, this temple was the one sanctuary place that we kept going back to.

00:15:09.012 --> 00:15:09.412
Delwath: Right.

00:15:09.412 --> 00:15:10.532
DM: Yeah, this was where

00:15:11.732 --> 00:15:13.332
DM: Rai had been for-

00:15:13.332 --> 00:15:13.552
Kenzo: Yes

00:15:13.552 --> 00:15:14.212
DM: ... many years.

00:15:14.212 --> 00:15:15.551
Kenzo: Yes, yes, yes.

00:15:15.552 --> 00:15:17.632
DM: And in the middle of the

00:15:19.292 --> 00:15:22.352
DM: building is a statue of Jade-

00:15:22.352 --> 00:15:22.361
Delwath: Oof

00:15:22.361 --> 00:15:24.212
DM: ... missing a hand.

00:15:24.212 --> 00:15:25.492
Delwath: [laughs] Do you think it's Rai?

00:15:25.492 --> 00:15:25.652
DM: The-

00:15:27.092 --> 00:15:27.102
Kenzo: Nah.

00:15:27.102 --> 00:15:31.952
DM: The, the features look worn, almost eroded, like you can't make out, um,

00:15:34.532 --> 00:15:39.712
DM: out details and, but you hear immediately a, a voice in, in your head.

00:15:39.712 --> 00:15:39.912
DM: Um,

00:15:42.072 --> 00:15:44.992
DM: "Did Dimataur find you, or did he send you?

00:15:47.512 --> 00:15:48.372
DM: What brings you here?"

00:15:50.472 --> 00:15:51.072
Kenzo: No way.

00:15:52.592 --> 00:15:52.912
Kenzo: Wow.

00:15:53.992 --> 00:15:55.452
Kenzo: Cool.

00:15:55.452 --> 00:15:55.812
Delwath: Yes.

00:15:55.812 --> 00:15:56.232
Kenzo: Uh.

00:15:56.232 --> 00:15:58.672
Seeker: Yes, we have met Dimataur.

00:15:58.672 --> 00:15:59.552
DM: Okay.

00:15:59.552 --> 00:16:00.472
Delwath: Apollyon's dead.

00:16:02.832 --> 00:16:13.252
Kenzo: Uh, Kenzo, uh, takes, takes the, the staff with, uh, Rai's hand on it and says, uh, "Uh, um, I think this is yours."

00:16:13.252 --> 00:16:13.732
Kenzo: And he,

00:16:15.412 --> 00:16:17.212
Unknown: uh, brings the, the hand over.

00:16:20.512 --> 00:16:23.232
DM: I think it makes little difference to me now.

00:16:25.852 --> 00:16:27.312
DM: [laughs]

00:16:27.312 --> 00:16:28.472
Delwath: He came all this way.

00:16:28.472 --> 00:16:30.152
Unknown: He came all this way to give you a hand.

00:16:31.672 --> 00:16:31.822
Kenzo: [laughs]

00:16:31.822 --> 00:16:33.312
Delwath: And you don't even want it?

00:16:33.312 --> 00:16:34.262
Delwath: [laughs]

00:16:34.262 --> 00:16:36.472
Unknown: He'll just go. We'll just go.

00:16:36.472 --> 00:16:36.911
Delwath: Fine.

00:16:39.512 --> 00:16:42.942
Delwath: [laughs] We struggled for...

00:16:42.942 --> 00:16:43.242
Delwath: [laughs]

00:16:45.632 --> 00:16:47.272
Wellby: No, no. Why, why a little difference?

00:16:50.752 --> 00:16:52.132
DM: Y- you do not...

00:16:52.132 --> 00:16:53.812
DM: He seems confused for a moment.

00:16:56.392 --> 00:16:58.792
DM: Dimataur did not bring my message?

00:16:59.892 --> 00:17:00.612
Kenzo: What was the message?

00:17:02.032 --> 00:17:03.702
Delwath: Wait, are we forgetting a message?

00:17:03.702 --> 00:17:05.221
DM: No.

00:17:05.221 --> 00:17:05.242
DM: [laughs]

00:17:05.242 --> 00:17:05.242
Delwath: Okay. [laughs]

00:17:05.242 --> 00:17:07.312
DM: Dimataur might have forgotten a message.

00:17:07.312 --> 00:17:08.792
Delwath: [laughs] Dammit, Dimataur.

00:17:08.792 --> 00:17:10.692
Wellby: Right. Have you met Dimataur?

00:17:10.692 --> 00:17:12.152
Kenzo: [laughs]

00:17:12.152 --> 00:17:13.832
Delwath: Di- um, Dimataur's, uh,

00:17:15.532 --> 00:17:16.492
Delwath: he's had some adventures.

00:17:17.672 --> 00:17:20.291
Wellby: He got old. It's been 30 years.

00:17:20.292 --> 00:17:20.872
Delwath: He, um...

00:17:22.592 --> 00:17:23.542
DM: He's doing well now.

00:17:23.542 --> 00:17:27.432
Delwath: He is doing well. Uh, we left him in charge?

00:17:27.432 --> 00:17:30.392
Unknown: In charge of the Circular Island.

00:17:30.392 --> 00:17:32.792
Delwath: [laughs] Uh,

00:17:36.052 --> 00:17:38.292
DM: n- no, too much to discuss.

00:17:38.292 --> 00:17:38.731
Delwath: [laughs]

00:17:40.212 --> 00:17:40.992
Kenzo: What was the message

00:17:42.092 --> 00:17:44.872
Wellby: that he was to have delivered?

00:17:48.612 --> 00:17:49.452
DM: There is...

00:17:51.512 --> 00:17:55.572
DM: [sighs] When we tried

00:17:57.692 --> 00:17:58.592
DM: some years ago,

00:18:00.192 --> 00:18:04.092
DM: a few years only I think, although time passes strangely here-

00:18:04.092 --> 00:18:04.132
Kenzo: 30

00:18:06.292 --> 00:18:10.684
DM: ... to- Close the portal to Limbo.

00:18:12.284 --> 00:18:15.794
DM: I brought a bunch of Dunmari monks into

00:18:16.844 --> 00:18:18.124
DM: this place, and I have

00:18:19.244 --> 00:18:20.684
DM: done the best I could to

00:18:22.484 --> 00:18:27.044
DM: keep them from fading, although, he stops for a minute.

00:18:28.744 --> 00:18:31.164
DM: See you have s- brought some back from the edge.

00:18:31.164 --> 00:18:32.504
DM: I, I thank you for that.

00:18:35.124 --> 00:18:35.384
DM: But

00:18:37.404 --> 00:18:39.144
DM: only a fraction of my effort

00:18:40.664 --> 00:18:42.084
DM: goes there because

00:18:43.564 --> 00:18:44.344
DM: nearby,

00:18:46.924 --> 00:18:48.213
DM: nearby as far as

00:18:49.984 --> 00:18:52.404
DM: distances in this place are concerned, which

00:18:53.844 --> 00:18:55.264
DM: has little actual meaning,

00:18:57.924 --> 00:18:58.824
DM: there is a

00:19:01.264 --> 00:19:02.664
DM: focus of stability,

00:19:04.544 --> 00:19:04.884
DM: a

00:19:08.124 --> 00:19:11.644
DM: seed of the material plane or something that has precipitated a,

00:19:12.764 --> 00:19:17.104
DM: uh, an island of order of a kind in this place.

00:19:19.764 --> 00:19:21.024
DM: And the entity that is

00:19:23.564 --> 00:19:24.584
DM: controlling

00:19:25.724 --> 00:19:27.204
DM: that seed has been

00:19:29.744 --> 00:19:31.204
DM: seeking to drag

00:19:32.404 --> 00:19:36.084
DM: Limbo and the material plane closer and closer together,

00:19:38.304 --> 00:19:40.584
DM: perhaps intermeshing them entirely.

00:19:43.504 --> 00:19:48.284
DM: And I have been trying to stop that, but we are balanced on a knife edge,

00:19:49.864 --> 00:19:54.324
DM: and I cannot leave here or the monks will die, and I cannot take them

00:19:55.464 --> 00:19:57.384
DM: from this place or...

00:20:00.564 --> 00:20:00.924
DM: Well, I've

00:20:02.764 --> 00:20:04.244
DM: no idea what might happen

00:20:05.304 --> 00:20:06.004
DM: should this

00:20:07.284 --> 00:20:09.984
DM: entity succeed in their goal, but

00:20:11.064 --> 00:20:13.944
DM: certainly it would not be good for the material plane.

00:20:14.964 --> 00:20:17.363
Delwath: Does the entity have the flavor of Cha'mutte?

00:20:19.564 --> 00:20:19.974
DM: No.

00:20:19.974 --> 00:20:21.364
Kenzo: What do you know of it?

00:20:21.364 --> 00:20:25.404
DM: This thing is far, far older than Cha'mutte.

00:20:25.404 --> 00:20:26.143
Kenzo: Oh, boy.

00:20:26.144 --> 00:20:27.824
Delwath: And I thought Cha'mutte predated time.

00:20:30.404 --> 00:20:30.724
DM: Yeah.

00:20:32.964 --> 00:20:33.764
Kenzo: Oh, boy.

00:20:36.024 --> 00:20:36.984
Unknown: Oh. There is a wound

00:20:38.804 --> 00:20:40.244
Unknown: at Isingue.

00:20:40.244 --> 00:20:42.664
DM: Yes, I know. That is what I went to close.

00:20:44.004 --> 00:20:47.724
DM: I realize now it was not a portal, it was something more complicated.

00:20:49.124 --> 00:20:50.784
Seeker: We've come to believe it's a vortex.

00:20:52.224 --> 00:20:52.564
DM: Ah.

00:20:54.224 --> 00:20:55.704
DM: It makes sense.

00:20:55.704 --> 00:20:56.664
DM: Is that why you're here?

00:20:57.904 --> 00:20:58.644
Kenzo: Indeed.

00:20:58.644 --> 00:21:04.244
Seeker: We've read that the way to heal it is from this side, not the other.

00:21:06.844 --> 00:21:13.784
Seeker: That we'll have to draw the Limbo activity away from the wound somehow.

00:21:13.784 --> 00:21:15.764
Unknown: With a piece of order.

00:21:15.764 --> 00:21:17.524
DM: Well, yes, of course.

00:21:17.524 --> 00:21:17.824
DM: That is,

00:21:19.204 --> 00:21:20.764
DM: that is what I told Dimataur.

00:21:21.864 --> 00:21:25.224
DM: Some powerful Dunmari sorcerer if he could find one.

00:21:27.324 --> 00:21:29.844
DM: Although only one of you looks Dunmari.

00:21:31.404 --> 00:21:34.204
DM: And he looks at you, and you do not appear to be a sorcerer.

00:21:34.204 --> 00:21:34.924
Unknown: I'm not, yeah.

00:21:35.944 --> 00:21:36.244
DM: But-

00:21:37.404 --> 00:21:38.344
Unknown: He's kind of

00:21:38.344 --> 00:21:41.424
DM: ... should not matter so much as long as one of you is...

00:21:45.064 --> 00:21:45.304
DM: Well,

00:21:46.844 --> 00:21:48.764
DM: it may be a challenge, actually.

00:21:51.724 --> 00:21:53.444
DM: I believe that this

00:21:56.044 --> 00:21:58.404
DM: fragment of stability is some kind of

00:22:00.624 --> 00:22:01.844
DM: hyper dense

00:22:03.324 --> 00:22:10.684
DM: series of runes that must be read in precisely the right order, and unfortunately, my eyes no longer work.

00:22:12.904 --> 00:22:14.144
Kenzo: Hmm.

00:22:14.144 --> 00:22:15.404
Unknown: Well, that's good news.

00:22:15.404 --> 00:22:17.444
Kenzo: Yeah, he's good with the runes.

00:22:17.444 --> 00:22:20.324
Kenzo: Uh, what do you know of this entity?

00:22:21.884 --> 00:22:22.824
Unknown: What more can you tell us?

00:22:26.664 --> 00:22:27.904
