00:23:05.504 --> 00:23:06.984
Unknown: Wait, is it the Orchard Keeper?

00:23:09.844 --> 00:23:10.004
DM: No. No.

00:23:11.964 --> 00:23:12.564
DM: [laughs]

00:23:13.904 --> 00:23:15.744
DM: The Orchard Keeper is something different.

00:23:15.744 --> 00:23:16.584
Kenzo: Mm-hmm.

00:23:16.584 --> 00:23:20.964
Delwath: The, the Orchard Keeper also was, we could have taken the Orchard Keep- I mean, the Orchard Keeper we knew could, right?

00:23:20.964 --> 00:23:22.464
Kenzo: Oh, right.

00:23:22.464 --> 00:23:24.704
DM: Plus, the Orchard Keeper was not...

00:23:24.704 --> 00:23:27.464
DM: Your inference is that the Orchard Keeper was from

00:23:28.684 --> 00:23:30.124
DM: somewhere totally alien.

00:23:30.124 --> 00:23:30.504
Unknown: Oh,

00:23:31.644 --> 00:23:32.144
Unknown: right.

00:23:32.144 --> 00:23:32.614
DM: Not from Limbo.

00:23:32.614 --> 00:23:33.504
Unknown: Not from Limbo.

00:23:33.504 --> 00:23:34.764
Kenzo: Right.

00:23:34.764 --> 00:23:35.124
Kenzo: Hmm.

00:23:39.804 --> 00:23:40.044
Unknown: Um,

00:23:41.204 --> 00:23:47.884
Delwath: right. So we need to go to this place, take this piece of order, bring it to the rift, use it to-

00:23:47.884 --> 00:23:48.504
Kenzo: Pull it back

00:23:48.504 --> 00:23:49.624
Unknown: ... pull it back.

00:23:49.624 --> 00:23:53.524
Kenzo: [laughs]

00:23:53.524 --> 00:23:54.584
Unknown: Easy enough.

00:23:54.584 --> 00:23:56.324
Kenzo: That sounds-

00:23:56.324 --> 00:23:58.824
Delwath: Yeah, like what, what could go wrong?

00:23:58.824 --> 00:24:00.224
Unknown: It's only the, you know,

00:24:01.544 --> 00:24:02.104
Unknown: original-

00:24:03.804 --> 00:24:04.904
Kenzo: Inhabitant

00:24:04.904 --> 00:24:05.754
Unknown: ... inhabitant of Limbo

00:24:05.754 --> 00:24:05.884
Kenzo: ... of Limbo.

00:24:07.044 --> 00:24:07.184
Unknown: So,

00:24:08.764 --> 00:24:09.724
Unknown: like, you know.

00:24:09.724 --> 00:24:11.084
Kenzo: How do we find this, uh,

00:24:12.564 --> 00:24:14.204
Kenzo: this piece of stability and order?

00:24:15.960 --> 00:24:19.300
DM: That is not hard. I can guide you easily enough.

00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:21.140
Kenzo: And once we're there?

00:24:22.840 --> 00:24:24.180
DM: Well, then you'll be on your own.

00:24:24.180 --> 00:24:27.380
DM: This is why I told Dimataur I needed help.

00:24:27.380 --> 00:24:31.840
DM: One alone can do little when I have two impossible tasks to achieve.

00:24:32.850 --> 00:24:34.800
Kenzo: [sighs] Yeah.

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:38.060
Seeker: Okay. What, what are the two tasks?

00:24:38.060 --> 00:24:39.080
Kenzo: Keeping the monks alive.

00:24:39.080 --> 00:24:40.920
DM: Keeping the monks alive and-

00:24:40.920 --> 00:24:43.080
Delwath: Right.

00:24:43.080 --> 00:24:44.080
Delwath: Closing the rift

00:24:45.660 --> 00:24:47.520
DM: ... closing the rift. Both require my full attention.

00:24:50.320 --> 00:24:50.740
Kenzo: Once we-

00:24:50.740 --> 00:24:52.240
Unknown: Wait. Sorry, go ahead.

00:24:52.240 --> 00:24:54.910
Kenzo: Once we, uh, engage with the entity,

00:24:55.940 --> 00:24:56.740
Kenzo: do you have any

00:24:58.160 --> 00:25:00.300
Kenzo: guidance or, or advice?

00:25:03.580 --> 00:25:04.980
DM: All I can tell you is this:

00:25:06.780 --> 00:25:07.700
DM: There are...

00:25:10.100 --> 00:25:11.720
DM: I have observed the

00:25:13.040 --> 00:25:16.700
DM: nature of life here, such as it is,

00:25:19.840 --> 00:25:21.020
DM: and I believe that

00:25:23.420 --> 00:25:23.800
DM: this...

00:25:27.080 --> 00:25:27.280
DM: Well,

00:25:29.540 --> 00:25:31.280
DM: there are things that live in Limbo,

00:25:33.240 --> 00:25:34.160
DM: but they are

00:25:37.200 --> 00:25:43.520
DM: so unstable and changeable that even as they grow larger and larger and more powerful, they turn

00:25:45.420 --> 00:25:55.540
DM: into nothing so much as great weather fronts that travel across the land but have no will or purpose behind them, or rather, it is better

00:25:55.540 --> 00:26:01.880
DM: said, their will and purpose changes from moment to moment such that they can never accomplish anything.

00:26:05.020 --> 00:26:08.220
DM: And eventually they grow so big that they fragment into tiny

00:26:09.540 --> 00:26:10.940
DM: motes of possibility

00:26:12.760 --> 00:26:13.660
DM: that grow.

00:26:14.820 --> 00:26:19.800
DM: Sometimes you will see what look like beasts moving through the landscape

00:26:21.640 --> 00:26:22.220
DM: that are

00:26:24.440 --> 00:26:30.840
DM: several of these filaments grown together, and they will eventually merge and grow into bigger and bigger

00:26:31.880 --> 00:26:33.940
DM: locuses of chaos.

00:26:37.160 --> 00:26:38.900
DM: My belief is that this creature

00:26:41.120 --> 00:26:45.820
DM: is what happens when one of these great chaos storms

00:26:47.040 --> 00:26:49.620
DM: passes over a locus of stability

00:26:51.320 --> 00:26:54.820
DM: and gains a fixed purpose and ability to control its form.

00:27:00.260 --> 00:27:02.760
Delwath: So hold on. Did, do we need...

00:27:04.200 --> 00:27:06.619
Delwath: The locus of stability itself is what we need, right?

00:27:06.620 --> 00:27:07.839
DM: Yes.

00:27:07.840 --> 00:27:10.300
Delwath: And that's what the runes are written on, you think?

00:27:10.300 --> 00:27:10.940
DM: Yes.

00:27:10.940 --> 00:27:14.080
Delwath: Okay. So we don't actually have to kill the creature.

00:27:14.080 --> 00:27:14.339
DM: No.

00:27:16.900 --> 00:27:16.970
Delwath: Uh,

00:27:20.080 --> 00:27:21.780
Delwath: okay. [laughs]

00:27:21.780 --> 00:27:21.940
DM: All right.

00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:26.150
Delwath: I mean, we might end up having to kill the creature,

00:27:27.980 --> 00:27:28.900
Delwath: but in theory...

00:27:34.770 --> 00:27:35.170
Delwath: Hmm.

00:27:38.060 --> 00:27:38.440
DM: Okay.

00:27:43.180 --> 00:27:46.020
Kenzo: Kenzo, uh, so th- this, the statue's speaking in our mind, right?

00:27:46.020 --> 00:27:46.200
DM: Yeah.

00:27:47.480 --> 00:27:48.740
